Third-party software in the dino release archives
==================================================

The dino binary is written in Zig and statically linked with no C library:
the code in it that isn't Dionysus's own is Zig's standard library and its
compiler runtime (compiler_rt), under the license below. The binary also
carries the Dionysus SDK's sources, which it unpacks for builds; they include
utest.h, which is in the public domain (second notice below).

Programs built with dino link the SDK and the C library zig provides for each
target (musl, glibc's headers, or MinGW-w64), whose licenses ship with Zig in
lib/libc. dino itself contains none of them.

